---
title: Proposition 22
---
order: 22
---
short_label: XI.22
---
statement: If there are three plane angles such that the sum of any two is greater than the remaining one, and they are contained by equal straight lines, then it is possible to construct a triangle out of the straight lines joining the ends of the equal straight lines.
---
red_highlight: yes
